      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely understandable to feel that clinical approaches don't resonate when you feel fundamentally hollow. Even if the \"old you\" feels distant, the current feeling of emptiness is real, and it's worth attending to because it signals a profound level of distress. Think of it less as \"saving\" something lost, and more as finding a way to make the current experience feel less unbearable. A therapist can help you find pathways to reconnect with your sensations, even if it feels small right now.",
      "source": "target",
